+This migration does not turn CLI equispaced samples into VR data. Use the
+existing MATLAB workflow for VR geometry exports. The caller-supplied-node
+C++ interface remains available for comparisons on identical VR coordinates.
+
+## Identity after fragmentation
+
+Original source labels identify retained support faces. Gmsh fragmentation can
+delete an original entity and produce several current faces. Its returned
+ancestry map connects each current face to its original support. Gmsh numerical
+operations use current live tags; extracted OCC calculations use retained
+original supports. Conflicting or missing ancestry is an identity error.
+
+Existing `tri_face_tags`, `scaffold_face_tags`, and edge-adjacent-face fields
+remain source grouping labels. They must not be used as live Gmsh handles.
+`mesh.meta` additionally records `cad_identity`, `occ_evaluation`,
+`native_identity_faces`, `native_identity_occurrences`, `runtime_version`,
+`gmsh_version`, and `occt_version`.
+
+## Unchanged limitations
+
+- The separate `same_support` heuristic and distance-based original-edge
+  selection remain unchanged. Exact face identity does not eliminate these
+  geometric searches or correct their existing limitations.
